course: dictionary
lesson: 2741
title: Disable: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disable is a verb, and it has three main meanings. Each one is about stopping something from working, but what stops it changes. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: To disable a feature in an app or on a phone means to turn it off so it does not work. «Disable notifications» means stop the messages from popping up. Check by swapping in turn off: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: To disable an alarm or a machine can mean to stop it working, often by damaging it. Disable can also mean to cause someone to have a disability through injury or illness. The word «disabled» describes people who have disabilities, so the context tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: Disable is a verb: disable, disables, disabled, disabling.
fact: «Disable» means to turn off a feature so it does not work, as in «disable notifications».
fact: «Disable» can also mean to stop something working, often by damaging it, as in «disable the alarm».
fact: «Disabled» can describe a person who has a disability, as in «a disabled person». «Disabled access» means a way in that people with disabilities can use.
fact: «Differently abled» is a polite, positive-sounding phrase that means disabled.
exercise: «Please disable notifications while you do your homework.» What does disable mean here? | Make them louder | Read them aloud | Send them to a friend | *Turn off so they do not pop up
exercise: «On a crowded bus, offer your seat to a disabled person.» What does disabled describe? | A quiet passenger | A broken bus seat | *A person who has a disability | A very tired driver
exercise: «The thief tried to disable the alarm by cutting its wire.» What does disable mean here? | Test it for fun | Make it ring louder | Paint it a new colour | *Stop it working, often by damage
test: «Young carers» help look after an ill or disabled family member. What is a young carer? | *A child who helps look after an ill or disabled family member | A new kind of bus driver | A teacher who runs a school club | A child who visits the doctor every day
test: Ella says «differently abled» sounds rude. What does it mean? | Very clever at maths | Able to fly without a plane | Not able to sleep at night | *Disabled, said in a polite, positive way
exam: Which word means the same as disable in «disable notifications»? | Read out | Wait for | *Turn off | Turn up
